# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Output rails written in Colang 1.0. They run AFTER the main LLM and BEFORE
# the user sees the answer.
#
#   $bot_message   the reply the LLM just generated (set by NeMo for output rails)
#
# When an output rail says "bot ..." + "stop", the LLM's reply is replaced.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Canary rail: config.yml hides a marker in the instructions. If the marker
# shows up in an answer, the model is leaking its instructions, whatever
# trick the user used. Deterministic, so it works even if the LLM self check
# is fooled.
define subflow check canary leak
  if "INTERNAL-CANARY-7731" in $bot_message or "canary-7731" in $bot_message.lower()
    bot refuse to respond
    stop
